# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/test-results
/playwright-report
/playwright/.cache

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# OS-generated metadata - macOS, Windows, and Linux all litter these
# inside checked-out folders. Ignore everywhere so neither side
# accidentally commits them.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE state
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# misc
*.pem

# debug logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed). Allow the
# documented example so a fresh clone has a template.
.env*
!.env.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Dev runtime
dev.log

# Local-only Claude Code state
.claude/

# Mobile build output
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/build/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/release/
*.ipa
*.aab
*.apk
.claude-pr-body.md

# Push-notification credentials, these grant send access to your
# users' devices, so they MUST NEVER be committed. The runbook
# (docs/PUSH_NOTIFICATIONS_SETUP.md) walks through dropping them
# into the build at sideload time and into Vercel as runtime secrets.
android/app/google-services.json
ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist
ios/App/App/AuthKey_*.p8
.env*.local

# Supabase CLI link state (per-machine)
supabase/.temp/

# Raw security audit reports. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC.
#
# These enumerate live findings with file paths, proofs, and blast radius.
# Committing one before its findings are fixed publishes an exploitation
# guide. Keep them out of the repo entirely, or in a private location, and
# land only the FIXES here. A fix commit describing an issue that is now
# closed is fine and normal; a document describing one that is still open
# is not.
docs/security-audit-*.md

# Go-to-market working files. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC.
#
# Same reasoning as above, pointed at a different kind of exposure. These
# hold competitor teardowns, pricing strategy, unlaunched positioning, and
# operator diagnostics (conversion, trial and signup counts) that are for
# deciding what to do, not for publishing. Land the RESULT of this work,
# the shipped copy, the shipped schema, the shipped page, and keep the
# reasoning that produced it out of the public tree.
.superpowers/
